  ('dae81486-811d-4a75-b5c7-b44ec6cd3033', '8af718c6-ca11-482b-9d6b-832f2b767928', 'bd32357e-c161-4052-abdf-a267b5139644', 'aedc9bf9-5810-404d-af31-095336b601fc', 'd9ec752e-e972-447c-b099-ccf502d554ab', '41e0a701-bdda-403b-bf4d-003aaffa605b', $qbx$Haryana’s per capita income is significantly higher than both Kerala and Bihar. Despite this, the IMRs of Haryana (28) and Bihar (27) remain high compared to Kerala's lower rate (6). This suggests that while economic development can provide resources, factors such as healthcare access and quality may still be lacking.$qbx$, 'comprehension'::question_type, NULL, NULL, 1, 5, ARRAY[]::text[], 'ai_xlsx_import_xlsx_2026-05-22T05-56-28-173Z', 'ba219b8a-c17f-46af-b642-be52f18c80ff', true, NULL, 4, NULL),
